// The GENERIC mutation rows: [file, what, find, replace, opts?]. They break files that you do NOT edit when you adopt the
// kit, so they stay as they are: build.js, test/unit-rule.js, the template's markers and the hover/active/focus CSS,
// the generic rules in fields.js (everything below its table), state.js, presets.js, controls.js, the core of format.js.
// Their finds are exact text of those files; if you change one of those files, the row tells you (CANNOT APPLY).
//   file     a src/ file name, 'build.js', or a test or tools path ('test/unit-rule.js')
//   what     one line: the behaviour that is broken (shown in the report)
//   find     text that occurs EXACTLY ONCE in the file (it is replaced once)
//   replace  the broken text; it must still parse and must change behaviour (see mutations.mjs)
//   opts     { max: N } raises the failing-test limit for a row on code that many tests use (say why in a comment);
//            { needsSnap: true } / { needsMark: true }: the row breaks snap (zero label, keyboard) or mark code, which only a project
//            with such an input can catch: mutations.mjs skips it when no FIELDS entry has `snap` / `mark`
// A row on a guard that your inputs can never reach is an EQUIVALENT MUTANT (it shows MISSED and no test could catch it):
// delete the guard from the code, not the test.
const BS = String.fromCharCode(92);          // a backslash, so this file holds no escape the tools might expand
